 :reviewed-invariants
 [{:area :trust
   :assessment "The closed trusted descriptor separately names :helper and :validator, requires different path strings and independently checks the validator helper hash in the seven-file inventory. Request input cannot select it. The validator receives the original request bytes and trusted pins, not producer-selected revisions; it calls full accept-response independently. Shared immutable laws are acceptable trusted context, not producer self-attestation."
   :limit "The two paths need not be separately installed releases. Writable-checkout hash snapshots remain convenience, as explicitly documented; immutable owner-controlled production artifacts are an assumption, not installed by this patch."}
  {:area :bounded-input
   :assessment "Validator decimal lengths are syntax/range checked before bounded reads, exactly both byte blocks and EOF are required, strict UTF-8 roundtrip preserves BOM identity, and request/pins use the restricted non-evaluating reader. Nonzero renderer exit or nonempty raw stderr never reaches successful validation. No request-selected load/eval path was introduced."}
  {:area :bounded-import
   :assessment "Private JSON has its own streamed expansion cap and strict native UTF-8 decoding. Closed shallow maps, bounded arrays, fixed enum mappings and tagged coordinates reconstruct the Result. No EDN parse, portable hash, portable UTF-8 traversal or canonicalization of output occurs on the parent loop after renderer spawn. Full semantic artifact checks belong to the pinned validator, so the shallow importer is intentionally not a substitute artifact validator."
   :limit "Native JSON.parse is not a duplicate-key/structural-budget EDN reader, nor is this public producer ingress. Its safety premise is the separately pinned fixed validator output. Its measured full-byte-cap import is not an arbitrary JSON-shape hard-real-time proof."}
  {:area :deadline
   :assessment "One performance.now deadline is assigned immediately before the renderer spawn call; timer delay is computed from remaining time. Validator does not receive another deadline. active! guards launch, close handling, copying/import and post-import completion. complete! independently checks the clock immediately before terminal CAS. An overdue callback cannot publish artifacts merely because the timer callback has not fired."
   :limit "Synchronous pre-spawn request admission still performs full rendering and is explicitly outside the spawn-relative budget. This review does not reinterpret the patch as fixing start!-entry responsiveness."}
  {:area :terminal-ownership
   :assessment "All spawned children are recorded separately. Cleanup first wins the terminal CAS, which suppresses validator launches and late success. Success is accepted only after the validator close event and reconciliation; the renderer was reconciled before the validator launch. Post-settlement cancellation cannot win terminal CAS or signal children."}
  {:area :cleanup
   :assessment "All unresolved records receive stdin destruction and TERM together, then KILL together after the shared grace, then one shared cleanup timer. Reconciliation requires child close and absent owned group; reconciled records are remembered, avoiding later signalling of their old PID. Remaining unconfirmed groups enter cleanup-holds and their read pipes are destroyed; new helper admission denies while holds remain."
   :limit "No deliberately unkillable live process or actual PID-reuse experiment was created here. Ordinary process-group cleanup relies on the documented OS/process ownership model, not a claimed kernel sandbox or pidfd guarantee."}
  {:area :closed-errors-and-retention
   :assessment "Validator exceptions are sanitized, raw stderr must be empty for normal acceptance, importer exceptions become fixed protocol-error, and arbitrary private error enums/coordinates reject. Settlement clears tracked raw output/error arrays and retained request bytes; stdin is ended normally or destroyed on cleanup. No raw diagnostic/secret marker is intentionally returned or persisted by these paths. Test fixtures exercise marker-bearing malformed messages and byte-channel negatives."}]
